From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:29:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: do not disable NAPI on SDIO devices

NAPI is only enabled on non-SDIO devices, but b43_wireless_core_stop()
disables it unconditionally. On an SDIO device the instance was never
enabled and napi_disable() waits forever for it to become idle, so
stopping the device hangs. Disable it under the same condition as it is
enabled.

Pointed out by the openwrt-ai review of openwrt/openwrt#25922.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5317,7 +5317,8 @@ redo:
 		b43_sdio_free_irq(dev);
 	else
 		free_irq(dev->dev->irq, dev);
-	napi_disable(&orig_dev->napi);
+	if (!b43_bus_host_is_sdio(orig_dev->dev))
+		napi_disable(&orig_dev->napi);
 	mutex_lock(&wl->mutex);
 	dev = wl->current_dev;
 	if (!dev)
